sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-daane-2021-pectoral-fin-to-standard-length-ratios> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Measured on 49 museum flying-fish specimens (3 species, standard length 1.68 to 24 cm), pectoral fin length is 0.406 to 0.823 of standard length (median 0.687), against 0.14 in halfbeaks and 0.088 in needlefishes (Daane et al. 2021, Data S1A)" ;
    dct:description "Status: supported (published measurements, re-tabulated; no new measurement). Daane et al. 2021 measured paired fin and standard lengths of beloniform specimens in the Harvard Museum of Comparative Zoology (Data S1A, 109 specimens in four groups). Pectoral fin length over standard length, recomputed from the length columns: flying fish (Cheilopogon furcatus, Exocoetus volitans, Hirundichthys rondeleti) median 0.687, range 0.406 to 0.823, n 49; gliding halfbeaks (Euleptorhamphus velox, Oxyporhamphus micropterus) median 0.274, n 19; halfbeaks median 0.14, n 22; needlefishes median 0.088, n 19. The paper's own reading: \"the length of flying fish pectoral fins increases rapidly\" with body size, the allometry \"was identical across the two- and four-wing flying fishes\", and the gliding halfbeaks are \"intermediate between halfbeaks and flying fishes\". This is the one flying-fish measurement set the genotype thread holds; it is proportion, which is what Daane's genes (lat4a, kcnh2a) are about. What it does not establish: Preserved museum specimens, lengths only: no body mass, no fin area or aspect ratio, no glide speed or distance. It does not establish any scaling exponent (no fit was done here) nor that the ratio is constant with size: flying-fish specimens under 5 cm SL have a median ratio of 0.645 (n 21) against 0.70 at 5 cm and above (n 28), so small juveniles are not simply scaled adults. Pre-registration: none: a published dataset re-tabulated for the Physics thread." ;
    delphi:context "Per-specimen rows in genotype/cache/daane2021_data_s1A_fin_measurements.csv; summaries in genotype/cache/daane2021_fin_ratios.json. Fetched from the publisher CDN after PMC answered the author-manuscript supplement URL with a reCAPTCHA page." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-daane-2021-pectoral-fin-to-standard-length-ratios> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-genotype-thread-claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-daane-2021-pectoral-fin-to-standard-length-ratios> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Pectoral fin length over standard length by group, from Daane 2021 Data S1A" ;
    dct:description "Computed by genotype/fin_ratios_table.py from the cached spreadsheet." ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Re-tabulation: pectoral_cm / SL_cm per specimen, then min, median, mean and max per species and group. No statistical test; no allometric fit was done here." ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/daane-2021-data-s1-fin-measurements> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom sub:map ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/genotype/data.json> .
